--- Scope / parity ---
Surface = native WinUI 3 port of web/src/components/a11y/VisuallyHidden.tsx in its cross-feature role:
the global screen-reader announcement region (web AnnouncerRegion in Layout, fed by useAnnouncer).
New code: the missing useAnnouncer pub/sub state-holder (IAnnouncer/Announcer, ZWSP de-dup), the ARIA
live-region semantics (LiveRegionSemantics = web liveProps), the AnnouncerRegionViewModel state holder,
PII-safe diagnostics (view.opened slug=VisuallyHidden), and a transparent ContentControl that composes the
existing atomic TsAnnouncerRegion (atomic primitives are out of scope per the prompt). No async data source
=> no loading/error/stale/offline chrome (same precedent as misc-surfaces/selectedVehicle + TourLauncher).

--- Pre-existing blockers repaired to make the gate runnable (documented, not silent) ---
1) apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj was committed-corrupted by its .gitattributes
   merge=union strategy (3 <Project> opens / 4 closes; unclosed ItemGroup => MSB4025 XML load failure), so the
   whole test build was red at baseline. Its own header documents the remedy: regenerate as ONE root with a
   single ordinal path-sorted, Include-deduplicated Compile union. Regenerated (887 unique includes, all verified
   present on disk) + 3 new SharedSurfaces\VisuallyHidden links = 890. Required to add this surface's test wiring.
2) apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/modals-dialogs/EntryDrawer/EntryDrawer.cs and FlagEditDrawer/FlagEditDrawer.cs failed
   to compile (CS0266): a predecessor added ModalsDialogs.DrawerSide (Drawer.Model.cs) which shadows
   Components.UI.DrawerSide at those two TsDrawer.Side call sites. Fixed by qualifying to Components.UI.DrawerSide.Right
   (value-identical; WidgetPicker/Overlays in other namespaces were already fine). Pre-existing, surface-independent.

