--- UIAutomation E2E capability note ---
TeslaSync.App.UITests (Category=UIAutomation, 147 tests) drives the PACKAGED app out-of-process over the W3C
WebDriver protocol via WinAppDriver/Appium. This runner has no WinAppDriver/Appium listener and no deployed MSIX,
so the suite fails fast BY DESIGN (the csproj states it is never silently skipped). These are repo-wide app-shell
E2E tests, NOT part of this surface (this surface adds zero UIAutomation tests). The required surface capability
(WinUI 3 / WindowsAppSDK 2.1.3 / .NET 10) IS present: the solution builds Release-clean and the headless suite is
fully green. Per the UITests csproj, the headless and UIAutomation suites are run independently; the headless
result above is the surface gate. The 147 UIAutomation failures are an environment/runner-infra gap, not a defect.

